From 3cdd1020f8848e20f1356718af30006a59ca4dda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:27:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(machine): per-axis direction in the machine file;
 inverted axes refuse posting until #374

A linear part of a .mch takes "direction": 1 | -1 (absent = 1). Anything
else refuses at load naming the axis. The machine model carries it as
AxisLimits::direction (machine::AxisDirection) and the project file
stores 1/-1, skipped when standard, so shipped machines, saved projects
and the post mirror are byte-identical. The travel check judges an
inverted axis's stroke in the machine's own coordinates (-v against
lo..hi), and the derived table box maps it to -hi..-lo. The machine
editor shows a per-axis "X+ moves: right / left" choice, applied
through the existing undoable EditMachineApply/LoadMachine command.

Until the post translates inverted axes (#374), the verification gate
refuses posting by name for such a machine, and so does the CLI post's
--machine door. Standard-sign code is never posted for it.

Fixes #373

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
